<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n88469" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσᾰγωγ-εύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>introducer,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. λημμάτων</span>”
				<i>one who hunts for another's profit, jackal,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					24.161
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				<u>Or.</u>
				28
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				49
			</span></i>).<i><span class="en">
				19
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				131
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>talebearer,</i> hence 'agent provocateur' of tyrants, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.522f
			</span></i>:—hence fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσαγωγίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, ἡ, 
				Dor.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποταγωγίς</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1313b13
			</span></i> (but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς καλουμένους -αγωγίδας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Dio</u>
					28
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.522f
			</span></i>).</div>
